<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's Cementos Diamante net falls.</title>
<headline>Colombia's Cementos Diamante net falls.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's Cementos Diamante SA y Subsidiarias suffered a steep loss in its net profit in 1996, a company statement said.</p>
<p>It said the 1996 net totaled just 15.9 billion pesos, down from 43.5 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>Operating income rose slightly, moving from 51.2 billion pesos in 1995 to 52.3 billion last year. But net sales dropped to 231.2 billion pesos from 239.4 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>Diamante was purchased last year by Mexico's giant Cementos Mexicanos (Cemex) last year.</p>
<p>((-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
